{
 "id": "2026-11-24-ariane-6-amazon-leo",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Amazon lost forty satellites last week. Today it risked thirty-six more. Did they make it?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Nine days ago, a Vulcan rocket from United Launch Alliance failed about ten minutes after liftoff. All forty Amazon Leo internet satellites on board were lost. Vulcan was meant to carry nearly half of Amazon's first network, and it is now grounded."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "This morning, Europe's Ariane 6 lifted off from Kourou in French Guiana, a day late after a ground-system problem. About two hours later, all thirty-six satellites were in orbit, Space.com and France Info report. That makes one hundred thirty-six on Ariane so far."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Amazon plans more than three thousand two hundred satellites. Only about four hundred are up, according to Space.com. The FCC, the U.S. regulator, wants the full first network in orbit by July twenty twenty-nine. Rival Starlink already flies thousands."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Amazon's network be complete by twenty twenty-nine? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
