 "upload": {
  "title": "Europe's Ariane 6 Puts 36 Amazon Satellites in Orbit #shorts",
  "description": "On November 24, 2026, Europe's Ariane 6 (flight VA271, Amazon Leo LE-04) launched 36 Amazon Leo internet satellites from Kourou, French Guiana, a day late after a ground-systems problem. It was Amazon's first launch since a ULA Vulcan failure on November 15 destroyed 40 Leo satellites. Space.com and France Info report the mission succeeded; it brings the number of Amazon Leo satellites launched on Ariane 6 to 136. Amazon plans more than 3,200 first-generation satellites; the FCC set July 30, 2029 for the full constellation.\n\nSources: Space.com, France Info (La 1ère), Arianespace, ESA, AstroSpace.it, CNES, KeepTrack, ULA, GeekWire, Light Reading.\n\n#tech #space #AmazonLeo #Ariane6 #satellites #ESA",
